laurel 2151: IOSurface placement follows the GPU state (2150) instead of boot-arg gpu=1, on top of area A's 2101. Order in create(): (1) backboardd's screen-sized BGRA surfaces (>= 700x1500: the Mi A3 720x1560) from the write-combined GPU pool only while backboardd's GL has the GPU (topaz_gpu_gl_active, asked per create); (2) the scanout path (cached slots, LAUREL SPOOL) only while GL is not loaded (asked per create, no longer cached at the first surface: GL loads after the first surfaces); (3) other surfaces: while GL is loaded the topaz reserve for screen-sized ones (contiguous, guard rows), then LAUREL SURF wired pages for all (no contiguous-first per surface; eagl copies such a surface into a texture), then contiguous memory below 4 GiB (mask 0xFFFFC000; kernel RAM now reaches 0x1AD004000, the GPU does not reach above 4 GiB) only while the GPU is wanted, then ordinary memory. The reserve buffers are below 4 GiB too.

